    <section class="intro-section">
      <div class="section-label">WHAT IS A DSCR LOAN?</div>
      <h2>Let the property's income help tell the story.</h2>
      <p>A DSCR loan is an investment-property mortgage that evaluates the property's qualifying rental income in relation to its housing expense. Instead of relying primarily on the borrower's personal debt-to-income calculation, the lender focuses heavily on whether the property's rent supports the proposed payment.</p>
      <p>That can be useful for real estate investors whose tax returns, business income, depreciation, or growing portfolio make traditional income documentation less straightforward. Lenders may still review credit, assets, reserves, experience, guarantors, and other factors.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="benefits-section">
      <div class="section-label">WHY INVESTORS CONSIDER DSCR</div>
      <h2>Potential advantages of DSCR rental financing</h2>
      <div class="benefit-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Property cash flow focus</h3><p>Qualification places substantial weight on the subject property's eligible rental income and housing expense.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Less reliance on personal income</h3><p>Many DSCR programs do not use traditional personal-income qualification in the same way as conventional mortgages. Other borrower reviews may still apply.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Portfolio-minded options</h3><p>Some programs allow investors to finance multiple rentals, with limits based on property count, total exposure, reserves, and program rules.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Purchase or refinance strategies</h3><p>Depending on the program, investors may use DSCR financing for purchases, rate-and-term refinances, or cash-out refinances.</p></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>Potential entity vesting</h3><p>Some programs permit eligible LLC or other entity vesting. Ownership, guaranty, and documentation rules vary by lender and state.</p></article>
        <article><span>06</span><h3>Options for different rental plans</h3><p>Programs may consider long-term rentals and, where specifically allowed, short-term or seasonal rental income.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="fine-print">These are potential program features, not promises that every loan includes every option. Credit, property type, occupancy, loan size, leverage, reserves, state law, and lender guidelines affect eligibility.</p>
    </section>

